---
import Adr from "../components/Adr.astro";
import Diagram from "../components/Diagram.astro";
import Excerpt from "../components/Excerpt.astro";
import Layer from "../components/Layer.astro";
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
import Path from "../components/Path.astro";
import Rule from "../components/Rule.astro";

const CI = ".github/workflows/ci.yml";
const SHARDS = "scripts/ci/pytest_shards.py";

const boxes = [
  { id: "change", x: 20, y: 30, w: 190, h: 60, label: "A change", sub: "worktree and branch" },
  { id: "hook", x: 250, y: 30, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Pre-commit hook", sub: "Ruff, mypy, Prettier" },
  { id: "check", x: 480, y: 30, w: 190, h: 60, label: "make check", sub: "local full gate" },
  { id: "vm", x: 710, y: 30, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Test VM", sub: "vm-run, IKI_VM_RUN" },
  { id: "changes", x: 20, y: 150, w: 190, h: 60, label: "What changed", sub: "docs or code" },
  { id: "shards", x: 250, y: 150, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Python shards", sub: "by measured durations", strong: true },
  { id: "harness", x: 480, y: 150, w: 190, h: 60, label: "pytest harness", sub: "containers, gate skips" },
  { id: "guards", x: 710, y: 150, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Generated-file guards", sub: "trees, core, bundles, Wasm" },
  { id: "jobs", x: 20, y: 270, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Other CI jobs", sub: "web, Rust, images, infra" },
  { id: "cluster", x: 250, y: 270, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Dev cluster", sub: "kind; e2e; restore" },
  { id: "ok", x: 480, y: 270, w: 190, h: 60, label: "CI passed", sub: "the one required check", strong: true },
  { id: "live", x: 710, y: 270, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Live clouds", sub: "gate every release" },
];
const edges = [
  { from: "change", to: "hook" },
  { from: "hook", to: "check" },
  { from: "check", to: "vm" },
  { from: "check", to: "harness" },
  { from: "vm", to: "harness", dashed: true },
  { from: "guards", to: "harness" },
  { from: "change", to: "changes", label: "push" },
  { from: "changes", to: "shards" },
  { from: "changes", to: "jobs" },
  {
    from: "changes",
    to: "cluster",
    via: [
      [115, 240],
      [345, 240],
    ] as [number, number][],
  },
  { from: "shards", to: "ok" },
  {
    from: "jobs",
    to: "ok",
    via: [
      [115, 355],
      [575, 355],
    ] as [number, number][],
  },
  { from: "cluster", to: "ok" },
  { from: "ok", to: "live", dashed: true },
];

const H = {
  short: "What has to pass, and where it runs",
  how: "From a change to CI passed, and on to a release",
  example: "A change to the oligo plugin's Chemistry tab",
  rules: "Gates, shards, browsers, generated files, clusters and clouds",
  ref: "Targets, jobs and decisions",
};
const toc = [
  { id: "short", label: H.short },
  { id: "how", label: H.how },
  { id: "example", label: H.example },
  { id: "rules", label: H.rules },
  { id: "ref", label: H.ref },
];
---

<Layout toc={toc}>
  <Layer n={1} title={H.short}>
    <p>
      One job, "CI passed", is the only required check, and it passes only when every job it needs
      passed or was skipped. A change that touches only docs runs Prettier and the docs tests; any
      other change runs every code job: Python in twelve shards balanced by measured durations,
      TypeScript, Rust, images, infrastructure, Slurm and a full dev cluster with a restore test.
      Locally, <code>make check</code> runs most of the same, and the test VM runs it off the laptop.
      Generated files are checked against what generates them, and each release waits for a live
      deployment to every cloud.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Monorepo with uv, pnpm and cargo workspaces and hardened CI (<Adr n="0019" />).</li>
      <li>Plugin action tests run fixtures through the worker (<Adr n="0093" />).</li>
      <li>Authorization is fuzzed with another project's objects (<Adr n="0101" />).</li>
      <li>Restores are checked, and tested automatically (<Adr n="0099" />).</li>
    </ul>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={2} title={H.how}>
    <Diagram id="gates" title="Where a change is tested, locally and in CI" width={920} height={375} boxes={boxes} edges={edges}>
      <div slot="change">
        <p>Work happens on a branch, in its own worktree; <Path p="CONTRIBUTING.md" /> covers the setup.</p>
      </div>
      <div slot="hook">
        <p>The pre-commit hook runs Ruff, mypy, the workspace imports on Python 3.12, and Prettier on staged files.</p>
        <p><Path p="scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="check">
        <p>
          Eight targets, in order; <code>make</code> stops at the first that fails, so <code
            >make -k check</code
          > runs them all. It refuses the browser opt-out <code>IKI_SKIP_BROWSER_TESTS=1</code> (<Adr
            n="0019"
          />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p="Makefile" sym="check: check-workflows" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="vm">
        <p>
          A machine that runs a full check off the laptop. The host-side wrapper gives each run its
          own id, sets <code>IKI_GATE=1</code> there, and fetches failing browser traces back. The VM
          itself, and <code>vm-run.sh</code>, live outside this repository.
        </p>
        <p><Path p="scripts/ci/with-browser-traces.sh" />, <Path p="CONTRIBUTING.md" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="changes">
        <p>
          A script decides whether a change is docs only. Plugin and template files, and anything
          under a <code>src/</code> directory, are never docs; a new branch or an unknown base runs
          everything.
        </p>
        <p><Path p="scripts/ci/changes.sh" sym="is_docs() {" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="shards">
        <p>
          Tests are of three kinds: plain, worker and browser. Each kind is dealt out a whole file at a
          time, longest first, to the least loaded shard, by the seconds each file took last time.
          A summary job checks every test ran in exactly one shard.
        </p>
        <p><Path p={SHARDS} sym="def assign(" />, <Path p="scripts/ci/test-durations.json" />, <Path p="scripts/ci/shard_summary.py" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="harness">
        <p>
          Postgres and SeaweedFS come from testcontainers unless the environment names them; xdist
          workers share one of each. Inside a gate, any skip not on an allow-list fails the run, and
          an <code>xfail</code> that passes fails it too.
        </p>
        <p><Path p="server/tests/conftest.py" />, <Path p="scripts/ci/pytest_gate_skips.py" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="guards">
        <p>
          Tests that fail when a generated file is behind what generates it: first-party plugin trees,
          the core plugin's app and migrations, bundled plugin components, and the rule that no
          <code>.wasm</code> is ever in git (<Adr n={[38, 114, 191]} />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p="spec/tests/test_first_party.py" />, <Path p="server/tests/test_core_plugin.py" />, <Path p="spec/tests/test_build_backend.py" sym="def test_iki_wasm_is_only_ever_built(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="jobs">
        <p>
          TypeScript (lint, types, Vitest, the generated client, the build and this site), Rust,
          the server, worker and plugin images, OpenTofu, dependencies and dependency review, and
          Slurm.
        </p>
        <p><Path p={CI} /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="cluster">
        <p>
          A kind cluster with the real chart, brought up headless by Tilt, then the end-to-end checks
          and the restore test (<Adr n={[14, 99]} />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p="deploy/dev/up.sh" />, <Path p="deploy/dev/e2e.sh" />, <Path p="deploy/dev/restore-test.sh" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="ok">
        <p>The one required status check: it fails if any job it needs is neither a success nor skipped. A new push to a pull request cancels its earlier run.</p>
        <p><Path p={CI} sym="name: CI passed" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="live">
        <p>
          A real deployment to Google Cloud and to AWS, checked and torn down. Never in CI: <code
            >make live-due</code
          > says which cloud's last passing run is behind the paths it tests, and a release tag
          refuses to build until each has passed (<Adr n={[97, 107]} />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p="deploy/live/live_runs.py" sym="def due(" />, <Path p="deploy/live-runs.json" /></p>
      </div>
    </Diagram>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={3} title={H.example}>
    <p>
      A change to the oligo plugin's Chemistry tab, whose source is <Path
        p="plugins/oligo/web/src/chemistry.js"
      />. Rebuild the bundle with <code>pnpm bundle:plugins</code>, which rewrites <Path
        p="plugins/oligo/components/chemistry.js"
      />; forgetting it fails <code>pnpm test</code>. Run <code>make first-party</code> after the
      last edit, since it records the plugin's current tree; forgetting it fails the first-party test.
      The focused browser test is <Path p="server/tests/test_oligo_components.py" />, in three engines
      with axe.
    </p>
    <p>On the pull request, the change script finds code, not docs, because plugins never count as docs:</p>
    <Excerpt file="scripts/ci/changes.sh" start="^is_docs\(\) \{" />
    <p>
      So every code job runs. The browser test lands in a browser shard, the first-party test in a
      plain shard, and the oligo plugin's action tests in the worker shard, through one test that
      finds every plugin with action tests. Shards are dealt like this:
    </p>
    <Excerpt file={SHARDS} start="^def assign\(" />
    <p>
      The oligo plugin isn't among the paths a live cloud test exercises, so <code>make live-due</code>
      wouldn't ask for one.
    </p>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={4} title={H.rules}>
    <div class="rules">
      <Rule title="The Python matrix" open>
        <p>
          Twelve shards: Python 3.12 runs five plain; Python 3.14 runs four plain, one worker and two
          browser. Browser shards may take 45 minutes, the others 30. One shard can be run locally
          with <code>uv run pytest -p pytest_shards --shard plain:2/5</code>. Files with no measured
          time are estimated from measured files nearby; the table is refreshed by hand from the
          summary job's output (<Path p={SHARDS} sym="def file_weights(" />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Browsers and accessibility">
        <p>
          Browser tests run in Chromium, Firefox and WebKit, and every page they visit is checked
          with axe for WCAG 2.2 AA, for content-security-policy violations and for page errors. A
          fixture fails a test when a press and its release land on different targets (<Adr
            n="0102"
          />, <Path p="server/tests/test_browser.py" sym='BROWSERS = ["chromium", "firefox", "webkit"]' />, <Path
            p="server/tests/test_browser.py"
            sym="def assert_clean("
          />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Plugins' action and upgrade tests">
        <p>
          A plugin's <code>ActionTest</code> documents run through <code>iki-worker run --local</code>.
          In CI, one test runs every first-party plugin's and the template's (<Adr n="0093" />, <Path
            p="server/tests/test_worker_local.py"
            sym="def test_first_party_plugins_and_the_template_pass_their_action_tests("
          />). Upgrade tests migrate sample data from an earlier commit and compare every
          revision's values (<Adr n={[94, 158]} />, <Path p="server/tests/test_plugin_migrations.py" />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Authorization fuzzing">
        <p>
          The access matrix lists every API operation; the IDOR tests call each with another
          project's objects, and every worker job route likewise (<Adr n="0101" />, <Path
            p="server/tests/test_api_idor.py"
            sym="def test_another_projects_objects_are_never_reached("
          />, <Path p="server/tests/test_worker_idor.py" sym="def test_every_job_route_is_fuzzed(" />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Live clouds">
        <p>
          The paths that make a cloud's live test due are the chart, the images and what they're
          built from, the deploy build, the plugins it installs, the worker, and server code the
          cloud decides; each cloud adds its own. Passing runs are recorded in <Path
            p="deploy/live-runs.json"
          />, and both the publish and release workflows start by checking it for the tag (<Path
            p=".github/workflows/release.yml"
            sym="live_runs.py gate HEAD"
          />).
        </p>
        <Excerpt file="deploy/live/live_runs.py" start="^RELEVANT: dict" />
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Nightly scale tests">
        <p>
          Imports, the grid, the queue and files are load-tested every night; the grid at ten million
          rows in CI (<Adr n="0103" />, <Path p=".github/workflows/scale.yml" />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="What this repository doesn't hold">
        <p>
          The test VM's machine and its settings, the lock that keeps heavy local runs to two at a
          time, and the split between a scoped gate for changes local to one page and the full gate
          for shared ones are working practice, kept outside the repository. Nothing here encodes
          them, so this page can't cite them. In the repository, CI's only scoping is docs versus code.
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Where the docs and the code differ">
        <ul>
          <li>
            The Makefile and <Adr n="0019" /> say <code>make check</code> runs exactly what CI runs.
            It doesn't run the dev cluster, the image builds, Slurm, dependency review or the docs job,
            and runs one Python version where CI runs two.
          </li>
          <li>
            <Adr n="0099" /> says the restore test runs on every change; the dev-cluster job is skipped
            for docs-only changes.
          </li>
          <li>
            The durations table lists four browser test files; about 35 files have browser tests, so
            most are placed by estimate.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </Rule>
    </div>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={5} title={H.ref}>
    <div class="refs">
      <h3>Make targets</h3>
      <Excerpt file="Makefile" start="^check: check-workflows" />
      <ul>
        <li><code>make check-python</code>, <code>check-web</code>, <code>check-rust</code>, <code>check-architecture</code> <Path p="Makefile" /></li>
        <li><code>make dev-ci</code>: the dev cluster, end to end, then the restore test</li>
        <li><code>make live-due</code>, <code>check-gcp-live</code>, <code>check-aws-live</code></li>
        <li><code>make core</code>, <code>make first-party</code>: regenerate what the guards check</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Workflows</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><Path p={CI} />: every pull request and push</li>
        <li><Path p=".github/workflows/publish.yml" />, <Path p=".github/workflows/release.yml" />: images and releases</li>
        <li><Path p=".github/workflows/scale.yml" />: nightly load tests</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Decisions</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><Adr n="0019" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0093" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0094" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0099" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0101" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0102" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0158" title /></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </Layer>
</Layout>
